# The backend image's build context is the repo root (see modules/backend/
# Dockerfile's COPY list: config.yaml, modules/backend, lib/, scripts/).
#
# data/ is none of that — it is the appliance's live state: intact.db, the fused
# graph sidecars, and the upgrade engine's temp dirs. On a box that has run an
# upgrade it is over a gigabyte, some of it root-owned, so `docker build` on the
# appliance failed outright ("error from sender: permission denied") and every
# successful build before that had been shipping the live case database to the
# docker daemon for no reason.
data/

# Never ship local operator state or build spoil into a context either.
*.upgrade-bak-*
__pycache__/
*.pyc
